<p id="mwATQ">In August 1975, following the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secondary_banking_crisis_of_1973–1975" title="Secondary banking crisis of 1973–1975" id="mwATU">secondary banking crash</a>, Barclays acquired Mercantile Credit Company.<sup about="#mwt143" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-35" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-35"}}'><a href="#cite_note-35" id="mwATY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATg">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwATo" aria-labelledby="1980_to_2000"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1980_to_2000">1980 to 2000</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Barclays&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: 1980 to 2000"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwATs"><a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Londres_-_54,_Lombard_Street.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwATw"><img resource="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Londres_-_54,_Lombard_Street.JPG" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Londres_-_54%2C_Lombard_Street.JPG/250px-Londres_-_54%2C_Lombard_Street.JPG" decoding="async" data-file-width="2816" data-file-height="2112" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Londres_-_54%2C_Lombard_Street.JPG/500px-Londres_-_54%2C_Lombard_Street.JPG 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAT0"/></a><figcaption id="mwAT4">Barclays head office after reconstruction in 1992 on a design by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GMW_Architects" title="GMW Architects" id="mwAT8">GMW Architects</a>,<sup about="#mwt146" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-36"}}'><a href="#cite_note-36" id="mwAUA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUI">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUM">]</span></span></a></sup> photographed in 2008 before subsequent remodeling</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwAUQ">Barclays Bank International expanded its business in 1980 to include commercial credit and took over American Credit Corporation, renaming it Barclays American Corporation.<sup about="#mwt149" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-37" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-37"}}'><a href="#cite_note-37" id="mwAUU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUc">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

